ili9881c: add the Luckfox 10.1-DSI-TOUCH-A ("10inch1") panel

The 10.1-DSI-TOUCH-A glass (ILI9881C, 800x1280, 2-lane) does NOT use the
0xFF,0x98,0x81 page switch the driver's ILI9881C_SWITCH_PAGE_INSTR emits; it
selects its manufacturer command banks (CMD2 BK0/1/2) through register 0xE0
(the E0 00 / E1 93 / E2 65 / E3 F8 gate). Driving it with any of the existing
0xFF-page descriptors (e.g. ampire,am8001280g used as a stand-in) leaves the
glass dark: the pipeline streams video but the panel's GIP/gamma/power are
never configured for this timing controller.

Add a new descriptor whose init[] is the verbatim vendor "10inch1" sequence
from the Luckfox Lyra SDK (rk3506-luckfox-lyra-ultra.dtsi panel-init-sequence),
translated 1:1 - every "15 00 02 XX YY" DCS write becomes an
ILI9881C_COMMAND_INSTR(0xXX, 0xYY); the E0 bank selects are ordinary 2-byte
writes, so no ILI9881C_SWITCH_PAGE_INSTR is used. A new .raw_init flag tells
prepare() to skip the trailing 0xFF,0x98,0x81 page-0 reset and the
set-tear-on wrap, which are wrong/unsolicited for this command model; sleep-out
(+120 ms) and display-on are still issued by prepare()/enable(). The mode is
the SDK "10inch1" timing (70 MHz, HFP40/HS20/HBP20, VFP30/VS4/VBP10); the host
DSI flags are kept at sync-pulse/continuous-clock, which is what the StarFive
cdns host already locks and streams (the SDK's burst flag is host-specific).

Same panel proven on RK3506 in the sibling luckfox-yocto project.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board/vendor-panel integration]

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-ili9881c.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-ili9881c.c
@@ -43,6 +43,14 @@
 	const size_t init_length;
 	const struct drm_display_mode *mode;
 	const unsigned long mode_flags;
+	/*
+	 * raw_init: init[] is a verbatim vendor DCS byte stream that does its
+	 * own bank selection (e.g. the ILI9881C CMD2 gate via register 0xE0)
+	 * rather than the 0xFF,0x98,0x81 page switch. Skip the driver's
+	 * page-0 reset + set-tear-on wrap in prepare() so the exact vendor
+	 * sequence is what reaches the panel.
+	 */
+	bool raw_init;
 };
 
